final class Repricer
{
    public function reprice(string $path): RepriceResult
    {
        $data = CatalogInput::readJson;
        $prices = CatalogInput::parsePrices($data);
        Validate: each price: model must exist in the DB: $em->find(Model::class, ['providerCode'=>p,'code'=>m]) — em->find for a composite? Model's PK is id. Use repository/findOneBy. Use ModelRepository? Simpler: $em->getRepository(Model::class)->findOneBy([...]).
        $em->transactional(...):
            $replacedIds = [];
            foreach prices: row = priceRepo->findOneByModelAndValidFrom(...) ?? new PriceRow(model,...) persist; row->apply(...); replacedIds[row.id()] = true
            $modelIds = distinct models' ids
            $events = usageRepo->findRatedForModelIds($modelIds);
            $delta = Money::zero(); $count = 0;
            foreach event:
                $newPrice = priceRepo->findEffectiveForModel($e->provider(), $e->model()->code(), $e->ts());
                if null → skip (в теории быть не должно)
                $offPeak = provider→offPeak
                $newCost = calc
                $oldCost = $e->money();
                $touched = ($e->priceRow()->id() is in replacedIds)
                           || $e->priceRow()->id() !== $newPrice->id()
                           || !$newCost->equals($oldCost);
                if ($touched) {
                    $delta = $delta->add($newCost->subtract($oldCost));
                    $e->repriceWith($newPrice, $newCost);
                    $count++;
                }
            flush
        return new RepriceResult($count, $delta);
    }
}
```

Note: delta is "the difference between the new sum and the old one" — delta over the events that were recomputed; only sum for the touched ones.

